# (working tree, 2026-11-20). Only change: --bg-obs builds the RTC/async prefetch observation in the worker
# thread with the inference, so rows keep executing meanwhile. Without --bg-obs it behaves like the original.
"""
RBY1 hardware policy rollout with websocket policy inference.

Connects to a websocket policy server, gathers live observations from
hardware (robot state, Aria image, hand qpos), and executes predicted
actions on the real robot and XHand grippers.

Observations are built from server metadata (camera_keys + proprio_keys), same contract as sim:
- robot0_joint_pos, right_arm, left_arm: RBY1 SDK `get_state().position` (Model-M slices)
- Camera tensors: latest Aria frame (shared memory), duplicated for every key in camera_keys
- hand_left_qpos / hand_right_qpos: last commanded 12-DoF values (replay; no encoder)
- task_id: one-hot via --task-id (default 1)

With `--dataset`, optional `--use-gt-action` (replay HDF5/LeRobot actions, no websocket) and
`--use-gt-proprio` (send dataset camera + proprio for policy inference). Same flags as sim rollout.
With hardware and a dataset loaded, the viewer briefly shows `get_state(INITIAL_STEP)` (same index as sim),
then prompts for `soft_reset_to` the first dataset action row (row 0) before the main loop.

Actions are dispatched to:
- Arms/torso/head/base: RBY1 robot SDK via send_joint_command_arms_head_base
- Hands: XHand replay process via shared STATE

Default --action-map-preset arm_hand_torso_44 matches a 44D policy (arms, then hands, then torso); override with --action-map.
Components not covered by the action map hold their initial pose; a warning is printed at startup.

Example (default 44D map, no --action-map needed):
python projects/rby1_teleop/rollout_rby1_policy_real.py \
        --host 127.0.0.1 --port 8000 --frequency 10 --aria_streaming

Example (custom 38D arms + hands):
python projects/rby1_teleop/rollout_rby1_policy_real.py \
        --host 127.0.0.1 --port 8000 --frequency 10 \
        --action-map "0:7->left_arm,7:14->right_arm,14:26->hand_left,26:38->hand_right" \
        --aria_streaming
        
0404 example:
export LD_LIBRARY_PATH="$CONDA_PREFIX/lib${LD_LIBRARY_PATH:+:$LD_LIBRARY_PATH}"
python projects/rby1_teleop/rollout_rby1_policy_real.py \
  --dataset //home/aloha/RB_Y1_workspace/EgoVerse/datasets/RBY1_human_data_0401_v8_egoengine/LeRobot \
  --demo-name 10 \
  --host 127.0.0.1 \
  --port 8001 \
  --frequency 4 \
  --action-map-preset arm_hand_torso_44 --visualize-eef-chunk --zero-obs --set-wheel-proprio-zero --safe-mode
  
if using Aria as input:
--action-map-preset arm_hand_torso_44 --visualize-eef-chunk  --aria-streaming  --set-wheel-proprio-zero
"""

